  "body": "Hands played: 53\nHand 53: Hero folds 33 preflop SB; villain holds 9dTs in BB.\n\nKey tendencies:\n- SB raise range WIDE: AdJd, JhTd, A6o, KsTo (4 observed) — not just premiums.\n- SB limp range: extremely wide, near-trash included (6hQo, Td8h, Js5s, 6h5s, Kh8d, Qd6d, Qs5h, 9s4c). ANY two cards.\n- SB call range: includes weak suited connectors/one-gappers like 6cQc, 9dJs.\n- SB fold preflop: 3 times (H14, H20, H32).\n- Folds to flop c-bet: 4/5 (80%).\n- Folds to ANY postflop hero bet eventually: 9/9 (100%) when villain checks first.\n- Villain postflop aggression: 8/8 times villain bet/raised postflop he had real equity (3x made hand, 5x strong draw semi-bluff). Semi-bluffs with OESD (~8 outs) AND flush draws (~9 outs) — ANY strong draw.\n- NO SIZING TELL: Villain uses same small bet sizing for draws AND made hands (flopped nut straight bet same as draw bets).\n- When villain CHECKS any street, he is weak — fire freely.\n- When villain LEADS or RAISES, respect it — he has made hand OR strong draw (~8+ outs). Hero should call with strong made hands on wet boards but fold marginal hands when villain RAISES.\n- BB range is extremely wide: Ts2s, 5d7s, 4sAc, Ks5d, 4d9s, Td6c, 6h5c, 5h5d, 7dKh, Jc3h, Qd7d, 2d6h, AcAs, 6dJd, 6hQc, 2s8d, 8cTc, 5c6h, 6hTs, 8h8d, 6sQs, 8hQd, 2dJh, 3d4c, 9dTs.\n- CRITICAL EXPLOITATION: Hero massively over-folding SB — folded 33 (H53!), A9o (H47!!), JJ (H41!), KAo (H35), KdAd (H5), TT (H19), Ad6c, Ad4s. Hero MUST open any hand worth playing from SB — this includes pocket pairs, broadways, Ax, suited connectors.\n- CRITICAL EXPLOITATION 2: Hero also over-folding vs villain's postflop bets on wet boards — should call/raise strong made hands vs draw semi-bluffs. But BEWARE villain may also have the nuts (H52 lesson).\n- BOARD TEXTURE MATTERS: On wet boards (connected/suited), villain may semi-bluff straight or flush draws OR have flopped a made hand. Hero should call with strong made hands (top pair+), be cautious with marginal pairs when villain raises.",
